# Article Workflow Gates

Apply these gates only when a request creates, substantially revises, previews, or publishes a Notion article.

- Read `.cursor/skills/notion-technical-writing/SKILL.md` and the relevant workflow before writing.
- New articles, security-sensitive articles, and multi-page series require a written plan and explicit approval before a Notion page is created or substantially replaced.
- Substantial articles require a Claim Matrix (research). Do not invent material numbers, model IDs, prices, benchmarks, or vendor-specific behavior; `low`/`Unknown` claims must not drive the main conclusion.
- New pages default to `type=Post` and `status=Draft`.
- Substantial revisions of `Published` pages use a separate Draft staging copy. Deploying reviewed content to the canonical page is a distinct approval gate.
- The parent owns Notion mutations; planning, research, writing, and review agents do not publish.
- The writer never reviews or approves its own article.
- Resolve every blocker and major review finding before site preview or publication.
- `Draft`, `Invisible`, and the site's article password are not confidentiality controls. Do not store confidential material in this site database.
- Changing `Draft` to `Invisible` requires explicit approval and a warning that the URL may be directly accessible.
- Changing a main article to `Published` requires a separate explicit approval.
- Companion pages use a stable slug, normally remain `Invisible`, and link through `https://ximouzhao.com/article/<slug>`.
- A requested Cover is generated under `public/images/covers/`, reviewed locally, uploaded with the approved Cover skill, and verified after attachment. Replacing any existing Cover requires explicit approval, including when deploying from a staging page to the canonical page.
- Fetch the saved page after every substantive mutation. Verify the public NotionNext route during Invisible preview and after publication.
- Do not create commits unless the user explicitly asks.
